---

### 4. Enterprise Terraform `.gitignore`

Copy and paste this into `.gitignore`. 

> **Certification & Interview Note:** Notice that `.terraform.lock.hcl` is intentionally **not** ignored. HashiCorp best practice—and a frequent question on the **HashiCorp Certified: Terraform Associate** exam[cite: 9]—requires committing `.terraform.lock.hcl` to Git so HCP Terraform remote runners use the exact same cryptographic provider hashes as your local machine.

```gitignore
# Local .terraform directories and provider binaries
**/.terraform/*

# Terraform state files (never commit state to Git)
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfstate.backup

# Crash log files
crash.log
crash.*.log

# Exclude all .tfvars files, which may contain sensitive secrets or credentials
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json

# Allow example variable templates to be committed
!*.tfvars.example

# Ignore override files as they are usually used for local dev overrides
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json

# Ignore CLI configuration files that may contain HCP API tokens
.terraformrc
terraform.rc

# Ignore binary execution plans (can contain plaintext secrets)
tfplan
*.tfplan
*.plan

# Security & local environment variables
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# OS & IDE metadata
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo